## REPOSITORY LICENSE ZONES

This repository is organized into two explicit license zones modeled after open-core infrastructure licensing:

1. **ZONE 1: Core Protocol Engine, Client SDK, Tests & Public Documentation** — Licensed under the **MIT License**.
   Includes:
   - `lib/index.js` (Zero-dependency Node.js verification SDK entry point & Express/HTTP middleware)
   - `lib/crypto.js` (Proof-of-work generator, HMAC seals, canonicalization, shared runtime/escaping helpers)
   - `lib/core.js` (Core verification engine, telemetry validation, rate limiting, replay defense)
   - `lib/telemetry.js` (Kinematic jerk entropy & pointer dynamics evaluation)
   - `lib/kv.js` & `lib/config.js` (Key-value store adapters and environment loader)
   - `src/tracer.js` & `index.d.ts` (Client-side attestation collector and TypeScript declarations)
   - `public/obsx.min.js`, `public/veritas.min.js`, `public/tracer.min.js` (Built client SDK bundles)
   - `public/app.js`, `public/notes.js`, `public/style.css`, `public/install.md`, public demo pages (`public/index.html`, `public/docs.html`, `public/notes.html`, `public/privacy.html`, `public/terms.html`), and static brand/icon assets in `public/`
   - `scripts/`, `tests/`, `docs/`, `.github/`, `README.md`, `README.baseline.md`, `SECURITY.md`, `package.json`, `.gitignore`, `.env.example`
   - Any auxiliary build, packaging, CI, or documentation file not explicitly listed under Zone 2 defaults to the **MIT License** (Zone 1).

2. **ZONE 2: Node Operator Scaffolding, Bot Protection, Auto-Updater & Dashboard** — Licensed under the **Elastic License 2.0 (ELv2) + Additional OBSX Zone 2 Terms** (see Part 2).
   Includes:
   - `server.js` (HTTP server harness, operator routes, and metrics broadcaster)
   - `lib/accounts.js` (Multi-tenant user and project key administration)
   - `lib/mailer.js` (Automated security incident notifications and email delivery)
   - `lib/botshield.js` (Origin shield, adaptive load shedding, body gating, and connection posture engine)
   - `lib/updater.js` (Upstream sync, CRLF-safe tree fingerprint attestation, license integrity verification, and Safe Mode checks)
   - `tools/flood.js` (Load shedding verification and origin stress test harness)
   - `public/dashboard.html` & `public/dashboard.js` (Node operator management interface)

