## TRANSITION & GRANDFATHERING POLICY (RELEASE v2.2.0+ & POST-CUTOFF)

1. **Grandfathered Self-Hosted Community Instances (Installed on or prior to November 15, 2026):**
   - Consistent with the Prospective Applicability rule above (which preserves MIT for pre-v2.2.0 releases), operators of standalone self-hosted community instances of v2.2.0 installed on or before **November 15, 2026** retain perpetual internal self-hosting rights for that installation without commercial fee under Zone 1 (MIT) and Zone 2 (ELv2) self-hosting permissions, while commercial hosted SaaS redistribution remains excluded.
   - Standalone self-hosted deployments must configure local secrets/keys and do not receive hosted Sentinel™ cloud entitlements without a managed or enterprise agreement.
2. **Post-Transition Clones & Commercial Restrictions (Cloned or upgraded subsequent to November 15, 2026):**
   - Deployments, forks, and upgrades created after November 15, 2026 remain subject to all Zone 2 source-available terms (ELv2 + Additional OBSX Zone 2 Terms) and Sentinel™ proprietary boundaries. Commercial SaaS hosting and extraction of Zone 2 components into competing products remain strictly prohibited.
3. **Integrity Verification, Safe Mode & Coordinated Disclosure Guarantee:**
   - `lib/updater.js` computes CRLF-normalized SHA-256 fingerprints across critical source files and `LICENSE`, tracking local license acceptance state and entering Safe Mode if critical integrity assets are missing or operator acceptance enforcement fails.
   - Security researchers and operators discovering bugs, false positives, or integrity discrepancies are welcome to report them cleanly via `security@obsx.tech`.

