## PART 2: ZONE 2 SOURCE-AVAILABLE LICENSE (ELASTIC LICENSE 2.0 + ADDITIONAL OBSX ZONE 2 TERMS)

*Note: Part 2 adapts the Elastic License 2.0 (ELv2) framework with additional OBSX-specific Zone 2 protections (clauses 3(b) and 3(d)–(f)). For unmodified upstream ELv2 text, refer to https://www.elastic.co/licensing/elastic-license.*

### 1. Acceptance
By using, copying, modifying, or distributing any software, algorithms, or files designated under
Zone 2—specifically including the node operator dashboard, server harness, origin bot shield, auto-updater, stress harness, and account/mailer modules—you agree to all of the terms and conditions below.

### 2. Right to Use
You may copy, distribute, modify, and create derivative works of the Zone 2 software,
subject to the non-negotiable limitations in Section 3.

**Permitted Uses Include:**
- Downloading and running the full self-hosted node as-is for personal, commercial, or internal enterprise infrastructure.
- Making private modifications and custom extensions for your internal, private operations.
- Inspecting source code, conducting internal security audits, and testing.

### 3. Limitations
You may not:
- **(a) Hosted SaaS Service Prohibition**: Provide the Zone 2 software, or any portion, feature, or functionality derived from Zone 2, to third parties as a hosted, managed, or software-as-a-service (SaaS) offering;
- **(b) Component & Algorithm Extraction Prohibition**: Extract, copy, adapt, or incorporate Zone 2 modules, UI components, or origin shield/metrics/account implementations into any competing commercial product or competing anti-bot/protection service;
- **(c) Notice Removal**: Move, change, disable, or obscure any licensing, copyright, attribution, or legal notices of the licensor;
- **(d) Sentinel™ Impersonation & Spoofing Prohibition**: Distribute or deploy any module claiming to represent, emulate, or spoof the closed-source OBSX Sentinel™ service or its proprietary cloud API endpoints (`https://obsx.tech`);
- **(e) Origin Shield Abuse & Harvesting Prohibition**: Abuse, spoof, or harvest the origin shield telemetry endpoints (`/api/v1/bot-protection`, `/api/v1/sentinel/ring`), forwarding header integrity checks, or connection posture telemetry to operate unauthorized scraping proxies, IP reputation bypass tooling, or commercial traffic relays;
- **(f) License Integrity & Safe Mode Tampering**: Disable, strip, or falsify license verification routines, tree fingerprint checks, or Safe Mode reporting in `lib/updater.js` for the purpose of misrepresenting modified software as an official OBSX build or evading license acceptance controls.

### 4. Termination
The rights granted to you under Part 2 terminate immediately if you violate any part of Section 3.

